# Solve-side one-shot cognitive-role runtime audit

- [ ] No import from `system.vein_analysis`, `process_absorb`, `enter`, DB, Redis, Seven, or solver_harness.
- [ ] Exact model UID is `glm-5-2`; effort is recorded as UID-encoded `high`.
- [ ] `--continue` and `--resume` never appear in argv.
- [ ] Every invocation uses a fresh workspace, dedicated config, export, and the preregistered retry index.
- [ ] When a qualification profile freezes the user-level `~/.config/devin/AGENTS.md`, its sanitized path, size and SHA-256 are verified before launch and copied into both launch and invocation receipts.
- [ ] `sandbox_requested` is frozen per experiment: sandboxed POC-32/33 and source-compatible no-sandbox POC-35 are never pooled.
- [ ] `dangerous`, with or without Devin sandbox, is never described as a security or filesystem-isolation proof.
- [ ] The file-producing no-sandbox profile does not deny the entire filesystem containing its own workspace; role authority is frozen in workspace `AGENTS.md`/`TASK.md` and checked against tool events.
- [ ] Network, nested AI launch, git and destructive command denies remain present even when broad path Read denies are absent.
- [ ] No gold/expected file name can enter the model workspace.
- [ ] Output bundle is append-once and sealed only after stdout/stderr/export collection.
- [ ] A process-start failure leaves a deterministic partial bundle plus quarantine receipt and cannot be silently relaunched under the same attempt ID.
- [ ] The exact DONE grammar is validated against the actual output SHA-256; a correct hash embedded in extra prose is not silently accepted.
- [ ] ATIF-v1.7 top-level `steps` are counted directly and each actual `tool_calls`/`tool_events` member is counted once; identifier fields never inflate event counts.
- [ ] Non-zero exit, timeout, missing output, and model UID mismatch remain visible negative evidence.
